FluidLite: SF3 loop-end check is off by one, and "repairs" the loop by
looping the whole sample.

Applied to modules/fluidlite (a submodule, so the fix cannot simply be
committed) by the root CMakeLists before add_subdirectory. Reported
upstream; delete this file and the apply step once it lands there.

WHAT BREAKS
-----------
Sustained GeneralUser GS piano notes repeat every ~2 s, quietly, like a
delay with very low feedback -- the whole sample loops instead of its
sustain loop. It hits some patches and not others (Grand Piano and Bright
yes; E.Grand and E.Piano no), which is what makes it look like a bad
patch rather than a loader bug.

WHY
---
In `fluid_defsfont_get_sample`, an SF3 sample is decoded and then:

    sample->start = 0;
    sample->end   = sampleframes - 1;      /* LAST VALID INDEX */

`loopend`, per the SoundFont spec, is the first sample AFTER the loop --
an EXCLUSIVE bound. FluidLite knows this; fluid_voice.c:1795 says so in
as many words:

    /* 'end' is last valid sample, loopend can be + 1 */

But the validity check three lines below the decode compares the
exclusive bound against the inclusive index:

    if (sample->loopend > sample->end || ...)

so every sample whose loop runs to the very end -- `loopend == end + 1`,
which is legal and common -- is judged "fowled" and repaired to

    loopstart = start + 8;  loopend = end - 8;

i.e. loop the entire sample. Most of GeneralUser's Grand Piano samples
loop to the end (their loopend equals the decoded frame count), so most
of them get this treatment; the E.Piano samples loop well short of the
end, so they are untouched.

MEASURED
--------
A held C4 on program 0, rendered 14 s and scanned for re-attacks in the
decaying envelope (a monotonic decay has none):

    before:  4 re-attacks, +1.6 dB, evenly spaced ~2.0 s
    after:   0
    fluidsynth 2.4.8, same bank:      0  (control)
    fluidsynth 2.4.8, the source SF2: 0  (control -- rules out the
                                          SF2 -> SF3 conversion)

diff --git a/src/fluid_defsfont.c b/src/fluid_defsfont.c
index c5aeefb..cd32d2d 100644
--- a/src/fluid_defsfont.c
+++ b/src/fluid_defsfont.c
@@ -660,7 +660,7 @@ fluid_sample_t* fluid_defsfont_get_sample(fluid_defsfont_t* sfont, char *s)
         sample->end = sampleframes - 1;
 
         /* loop is fowled?? (cluck cluck :) */
-        if (sample->loopend > sample->end ||
+        if (sample->loopend > sample->end + 1 ||
             sample->loopstart >= sample->loopend ||
             sample->loopstart <= sample->start) {
           /* can pad loop by 8 samples and ensure at least 4 for loop (2*8+4) */
